From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:17:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: isp: boot the T8132 firmware again when
 a boot fails

On the J604 (M4 MacBook Pro 14", T8132) the first camera stream after
system boot fails: the camera detection boots the firmware and powers
the ISP down, and the stream's boot after it gets no first magic
number (-ENODEV) whether it follows at once (1.902) or 1.5 s later
(1.905, with the least off time). The next open boots, as does every
open after it. The boot that works follows a failed stage 1; the boot
that fails follows a full firmware stop.

Until the cause is known, boot again from apple_isp_firmware_boot(),
at most twice on T8132: the failed boot has powered the ISP down, so
drop and take the runtime PM reference again, as the second open does.
The stream then starts on the first open. Not for resident firmware,
which cannot be restarted.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c |  2 ++
 drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.h |  2 ++
 drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-fw.c  | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c
index a45c098070..64505aaae8 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c
@@ -1332,6 +1332,8 @@ static const struct apple_isp_hw apple_isp_hw_t8132 = {
 	.macos_session_settings = true,
 	/* macOS keeps it down at least about 1.2 s between two boots */
 	.min_off_ms = 1500,
+	/* Its first stream after the detection fails stage 1 once (1.902, 1.905) */
+	.boot_retries = 2,
 };
 
 /*
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.h b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.h
index a38ad70ec9..78d71b9e8b 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.h
@@ -318,6 +318,8 @@ struct apple_isp_hw {
 	bool macos_session_settings;
 	/* Least time the ISP stays powered down before it is powered up again, in ms */
 	unsigned int min_off_ms;
+	/* Boot again after a failed firmware boot, this many times at most */
+	unsigned int boot_retries;
 };
 
 enum isp_sensor_id {
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-fw.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-fw.c
index b9e6a52278..8275eb84bc 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-fw.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-fw.c
@@ -1396,6 +1396,7 @@ static int isp_check_restarted(struct apple_isp *isp)
 int apple_isp_firmware_boot(struct apple_isp *isp)
 {
 	bool restart = isp->hw->resident_fw && isp->fw.started;
+	unsigned int tries = 0;
 	int err;
 
 	switch (isp->fw_state) {
@@ -1410,6 +1411,7 @@ int apple_isp_firmware_boot(struct apple_isp *isp)
 		return -EIO;
 	}
 
+again:
 	/* The firmware starts with new rings. */
 	isp->ipc_stale = NULL;
 	isp->ipc_failed = false;
@@ -1427,6 +1429,18 @@ int apple_isp_firmware_boot(struct apple_isp *isp)
 		if (err)
 			isp_firmware_shutdown(isp);
 	}
+	if (err && !isp->hw->resident_fw && tries < isp->hw->boot_retries) {
+		/*
+		 * On T8132 the first boot after the camera detection gets no
+		 * first magic number, and the next one starts. The failed
+		 * boot powered the ISP down: cycle it as a second open does.
+		 */
+		tries++;
+		dev_warn(isp->dev, "firmware boot failed: %d; booting again (%u of %u)\n",
+			 err, tries, isp->hw->boot_retries);
+		pm_runtime_put_sync(isp->dev);
+		goto again;
+	}
 	if (err) {
 		dev_err(isp->dev, "failed to boot firmware: %d\n", err);
 		pm_runtime_put_sync(isp->dev);
@@ -1435,6 +1449,8 @@ int apple_isp_firmware_boot(struct apple_isp *isp)
 		return err;
 	}
 
+	if (tries)
+		dev_info(isp->dev, "firmware booted on try %u\n", tries + 1);
 	isp->fw_state = ISP_FW_RUNNING;
 
 	return 0;
-- 
2.43.0

